config/settings.yaml.bak_pre_B1_htfboost_20260720:348:              updown_hold_winners_to_resolution: false  # 2026-07-17 operator+Codex GO: xrp 1h|up was 1 of only TWO xrp lanes with NO per-lane exit tuning (2 keys vs 5-13 on every sibling) and they are the only two bleeding. hold=true GATES BOTH exits (live_testing.py:528): take_profit never fires and green positions can't flatten => 0 TP exits across 54 trades, while the hold=false DOWN siblings on the SAME asset bank 12 (15m) and 3 (1h) TPs and are green. Worst losses were all GREEN FIRST: 15m|up -$11.58 (+21% mfe -> 0.12); 1h|up -$5.06 (+44% -> 0.00), -$5.05 (+17% -> 0.00) = -$21.69 over 3 trades vs -$10.82 combined net. xrp 1h|up reaches resolution only 3/37 so hold_winners harvests ~no resolution edge here, unlike btc/doge 1h|up (mfe p50 +29.8%, +$16.62) whose give-back is NOT trail-fixable (07-13, 07-16 Prop-A) — and this is a TP, not a trail. CALIBRATION not proven-optimization (Codex). xrp 5m + asset-level UNTOUCHED (5m|up inherits asset-level stop_cents; 5m carries ~$300). Break: revert true if positive-MFE-to-stop failures don't drop over 15-20 new closes.
