config/settings.yaml.bak_pre_B1_htfboost_20260720:1921:            entry_window_max: 15  # 2026-07-17 operator+Codex GO (SELECTIVE cap): was 32.0 -> 15 = the window's own span, so this lane can only trade a LIVE market. PRE-WINDOW ENTRIES PROVEN: ENTRY.minutes_to_market_end>15 on a 15-MINUTE market means the window had not opened; falsified 176/176 with 0 counter-examples (market_question start vs entry ts; leads up to +64min — bot bought 4 different eth 15m windows in one minute at 06:39). Aggregate 15m: IN n=200 WR46% +$195.27 vs PRE n=189 WR37% -$110.42; the 15-30min bucket alone = n=143 WR29% -$135.12 (largest loss pool in the session). THIS LANE: IN n=41 WR51% +$48.87 vs PRE n=15 WR27% -$8.99. 5m lanes already do this implicitly (entry_window_max 4.0-4.5 < 5-min span) and win 53% — that is WHY 5m outperforms 15m/1h, not exits or asset. btc|15m|down is already capped at 15 and is the best 15m lane. Operator accepted the frequency cut (~48% of 15m volume). 5m + 1h + asset-level UNTOUCHED; eth|15m|up and xrp|15m|down EXCLUDED per Codex (their pre-window cohorts are positive/noise). Break: revert 32.0 if IN-window WR drops below the pre-cap blended WR over the next 15-20 closes, or the lane starves >24h.
