config/settings.yaml:472:    tp_giveback_enabled: false  # 2026-08-11 RIPPED (operator: "rip out the bullshit bandaids I don't need"). Feed-blind: proven this session it MISSES the give-backs it was built for (every big BNB give-back had mae==exit = no intervening tick observed, so a reactive trail can't bank a retrace it never sees). Confirmed-peak/green-floor sub-patches are now dead code (fire-condition first clause is self._tp_giveback_enabled). The ever-green MFE stop is the real exit fix and stays ON.  # 2026-08-10 RE-ENABLED (operator: "+108 to nothing is not okay"). The 08-09 off-decision was made on 4 fires, 2 of which were the RARE settlement-gap failure. Re-measured on the FULL log: of 200 give-backs (peak>=30% then lost), 96% are WALK-DOWNS the trail banks; only 4% are gaps. Both live BNB give-backs (1h YES peak +108% and +72%) are walk-downs -> trail converts -$15.21 to +$15.68 (+$31 swing). Only the 2 bitcoin-15m fade give-backs gap (trail misses those; separate fix). STAGED (frozen at init) -> rides the MFE-cond restart. WATCH first live fires bank real green.  # 2026-08-09 ENABLED (operator GO). ROOT of the deep-loss bleed: 74% of Aug catastrophic-stops were EVER-GREEN round-trips (median peaked +50% -> died -65%); 77 Aug losses peaked >=+30% then round-tripped (-$611). This banks a reversing winner on a >=retrace(0.20) from peak(>=arm 0.30) => exits >=+10% green instead of riding to -55%/-68% catastrophic. Fires UNDER hold (reason take_profit_giveback NOT in the hold-enforce suppression tuple). Only fires on a REAL retrace so a still-climbing runner is never cut (the 07-13/07-16 fixed-trail failure mode is avoided). Projected +~$977 swing on the 77 round-trip losses. WATCH first fires = banking real green not phantom-mark noise.
