config/settings.yaml:2346:  override_file: data/runtime/claude_direction_override.json
config/settings.yaml:2350:# ── FAVORITE-LONGSHOT lane (08-07) ──────────────────────────────────────────
config/settings.yaml:2353:# underpriced (favorite-longshot bias) so this is +EV with NO direction prediction.
config/settings.yaml:2356:  # 08-08 RE-ENABLED (operator caught the confound): the earlier "cut, it's a loser" read
config/settings.yaml:2357:  # was measured while the exit-BLINDNESS bug was live — it inflated losses to -$70 (vs -$35
config/settings.yaml:2360:  # favorites with working exits and judge on CLEAN data. Freshness was ruled out (losers had
config/settings.yaml:2362:lane_tape_adapter:
config/settings.yaml:2363:  mode: "live"                # 2026-08-11 REALIZED SIZING LIVE (operator: results, not shadow). min_mult 0.25/max_mult 1.0 => DE-SIZE realized losers to as low as 25% bet, NEVER upsizes; winner-protected (avg_pnl>=0 never cut) + green-gated (only cuts lanes that STOPPED going green). Shrinks the band-long bleed the adapter already flags (hype15m/bitcoin5m up) and self-lifts when a lane recovers. Revert mode:"off" to disable.
config/settings.yaml:2364:  admission_mode: "live"      # 2026-08-08 PLUG IN THE REALIZED SELF-FLIPPING BRAIN. Was default-off, so every gate calling get_tape_admission_delta() (eth/btc/sol min_edge + favorite sit-out) read a hardcoded 0.0 = tape-blind. Per-(asset|window|side) delta from the last k realized closes: >0 tightens a net-losing/never-green side, <0 loosens a winning+green side; flips sign automatically as the tape turns.
config/settings.yaml:2365:  window_closes: 6            # rolling realized closes per lane (fast reaction)
config/settings.yaml:2368:  green_keep_rate: 0.5        # a net-losing lane still hitting green >=50% is variance, not tape-turn -> not de-admitted
config/settings.yaml:2374:favorite_lane:
config/settings.yaml:2377:  window_floors:         # 2026-08-10 PER-WINDOW FLOOR (operator "improve if data offers a filter, else cut"). 1h favorites split (n=29, 8 sess): 0.85-0.89 = 50% WR net -$65 (a 1h fav has a full HOUR to cross back through strike => 0.86 is a coin-flip); 0.90-0.94 = 72.7% WR net +$3.88 (clears 68% breakeven). 15m favs win 87% at 0.85 (net +$175 — UNTOUCHED). Raise ONLY 1h's floor. Turns 1h favs -$61 -> ~breakeven+. Absent/per-tf-absent => uses `floor` (byte-identical). Hot-reloads (read in _favorite_lane_signals via full_config.get each scan).
config/settings.yaml:2379:  price_max: 0.93        # 08-07 HUGE-LOSS FIX: skip DEEP favorites (>=0.93). A 0.96 fav pays ~4% per win but loses ~96% of stake when it gaps to $0 at settlement (the xrp -$70.37 was entry 0.96) — worst risk/reward. The 0.85-0.93 band pays enough per win (~9-18%) to survive its own loss ratio.
config/settings.yaml:2380:  size_usd: 25.0         # 2026-08-10 ROLLED BACK 70->25 (operator, longevity/Kelly): favorites are Kelly-NEGATIVE (p0.77 b0.29 => f*=-0.02) so $70=7% of bankroll on a -EV lane = ruin risk. +869 baseline had NO fav lane + $25 max. $25 base; per-lane winners upsized via adaptive_sizer (proven_lane_max_usd 40).
config/settings.yaml:2381:  size_taper_enabled: true   # 2026-08-09 #2 SIZE-TAPER (operator GO): scale stake by payoff (1-fav_price)/(1-floor); 0.85 fav=full, 0.93 fav=~0.47x. Scope: 0.88-0.91 band 71%WR but -$111 (thin payoff); recovers ~+$50, zero trades cut. RESTART-CLASS (code).
config/settings.yaml:2384:  sit_out_trend_aligned_mode: shadow   # 2026-08-09 #1 (operator GO, SHADOW-first): favorites bet WITH a trending tape BLEED (-$365); FLAT/against-trend WIN. shadow=log would-sit-out only (still trades); live=sit out aligned; off=byte-identical. Flip to live after shadow confirms.
config/settings.yaml:2385:  windows: [15m, 1h]     # 08-08 15m RESTORED: the earlier "cut 15m, it bled -$185" was the SAME confound — those -$70 15m losses were the exit-BLINDNESS bug (settlement gap-through skipped the cap), not a 15m-lane defect. With _mark_delta_blind_skip() live those cap at ~-$35. Re-test both windows on clean data before cutting anything.
config/settings.yaml:2387:  presettle_derisk_secs: 180     # 08-07 HUGE-LOSS FIX (the gap-through): a %-stop CANNOT catch a favorite gapping 0.85->$0 in the final settlement candle (the sol -$70.81 entry 0.87 rode to RESOLVED:NO). In the final N secs, if a favorite's mark has FLIPPED to <= presettle_derisk_price (i.e. it's now the underdog = losing), exit to salvage instead of $0. Winners mark toward 1.0 near settlement so they're never touched. 0 => disabled. 08-08 NUDGE 120->180: give slower 1h favorites more runway to be caught.
config/settings.yaml:2388:  presettle_derisk_price: 0.55   # 08-08 NUDGE 0.5->0.55: the bnb 1h loser expired at mark ~0.53 (entry 0.88, -40%), JUST above the 0.5 threshold, so the de-risk missed it (updown_expired -$32.39). 0.55 catches a favorite that has slipped to a coinflip-ish underdog. Still well below a winning favorite (>0.6), so it won't cut winners.
config/settings.yaml:2389:  hard_stop_price: 0.70    # 2026-08-08 06:1x DISABLED (was 0.70) — AUTOWAKE REVERT, it cut WINNERS 3-for-3 in its first 4 minutes live. Session test_20260808_060714, the 9:00-9:15AM ET window: sol entry 0.86 cut 0.695 -$15.41 | btc entry 0.90 cut 0.415 -$39.75 (the paged bust) | xrp entry 0.86 cut 0.675 -$17.09 = -$72.25 realized. CLOB prices-history says ALL THREE Up tokens settled 0.995 (WON): sol 0.875->0.685 dip->0.995, btc 0.705->0.755->0.995, xrp whipsaw->0.995. doge (control, same window, never dipped below 0.90) was never cut and won. A 15m favorite bought at 0.85-0.93 routinely dips to 0.60-0.70 mid-window and still settles 1.0 — a 0.70 mark stop is structurally guaranteed to cut the lane's winners, which IS the lane's 94%-WR edge (hold to resolution). The btc one is worse still: it fired on mark 0.415 (best_bid 0.41/ask 0.42, ws age 6.9ms) at 13:09:44 when the real tape was ~0.62-0.755 — a mark that never existed, after 106s where the position was invisible to check_exits (mfe=0.0, mae==exit pnl => not one intervening tick was evaluated). 0 => off; loss control reverts to hold_catastrophic_stop_pct -55% + the presettle de-risk above (the config the proven favorite lane ran in). Do NOT re-enable without evidence from settled favorites that a mid-window dip below 0.70 actually predicts a LOSS.
config/settings.yaml:2390:  early_stop_windows: [1h]  # 2026-08-09 RESTORED to [1h] (was reverted to [all] by the baseline restore, which re-armed the fast-window winner-cutter; it fired once this session on xrp 15m entry 0.91 -> cut 0.665 -$20.60, the session's biggest single loss = the exact documented failure mode). [1h] = 5m/15m ride to resolution, only doge-1h keeps the stop. STAGED not restarted. 2026-08-08 WINDOW-CONDITIONAL EARLY STOPS (operator GO; held-projection this session). The early hold-lane cuts — favorite_hard_stop (above) AND the independent hold_catastrophic_stop backstop — fire ONLY on these windows; other windows ride to resolution. Default 1h. WHY: the stop-hold sweep (this session) showed 5m/15m winners routinely dip to -20..-46% MAE mid-window and STILL settle GREEN (sol 15m held +114.73 vs stopped +105.65; xrp 15m +131.86 vs +124.02; hype 15m +83.84 vs +78.72) — so a mark stop on fast windows is structurally guaranteed to cut winners (this is the SAME finding as the autowake 15m bust note on hard_stop_price above). doge 1h is the LONE lane where HOLDING LOSES (-26.62 vs +8.49 stopped, delta -35.11) => 1h KEEPS the stop. The final-seconds presettle de-risk is a SEPARATE block and stays active on every window. Tokens: "all" => keep stop on every window (pre-change behavior); [] => keep it nowhere. RESTART-CLASS (execution code, not hot-reloadable).
config/settings.yaml:2391:  tape_sit_out_delta: 0.02  # 2026-08-08 REALIZED TAPE DEFERENCE: sit out a favorite side while get_tape_admission_delta(asset,window,side) >= this (side net-losing/never-green in CURRENT tape). Self-flips with the tape; both sides losing (chop) => both sit out. Needs lane_tape_adapter.admission_mode: live. 0 => off.
config/settings.yaml:2392:  respect_ai_direction: true  # 2026-08-08 favorite lane HONORS the AI direction driver (was side-agnostic, ignored it): AI FLAT/sit-out => skip asset; AI LONG => only UP favorites; AI SHORT => only DOWN. Kills the sol whipsaw (AI said sol=FLAT, favorite bought both sides+lost). false => legacy side-agnostic.
config/settings.yaml:2393:  fav_net_sit_out_avg: -1.0   # 2026-08-10 FAVORITE-SCOPED REALIZED-NET SIT-OUT (operator GO). Sit out a favorite (asset,window,side) while its rolling AVG realized net per favorite close <= this ($/trade). Reads favorite_net_tracker (FAVORITE-only closes, entry>=floor, keyed asset|window|side) — NOT lane_tape_adapter (which mixes favorite+band + is MFE/green not NET, so it read sol|15m|up as loosen while it bled -$99). Payoff-trap aware (favorites are high-WR/neg-NET). Validated on journal: -1.0 sits out doge15mDOWN(-6.3) xrp15mUP(-4.4) bnb1hUP(-3.5) sol1hDOWN(-2.2) etc; KEEPS xrp1h(+6.6) sol15mUP(+3.5). Self-flips: rolling window rolls losers off / recovery re-admits. null/absent => OFF (fail-open). RESTART-CLASS (favorite_lane not hot-reloadable).
config/settings.yaml:2394:  fav_net_window: 12          # rolling window: last N favorite closes per lane
config/settings.yaml:2395:  fav_net_min_samples: 5      # need >= N favorite closes before the gate emits a signal (else fail-open/admit)
config/settings.yaml:2397:  prompt_version: lane-feedback-v2-decisive
