config/settings.yaml:2515:  favorite_lane_enabled: false   # 2026-08-10 KILL THE FAVORITE LANE (operator: revert to +869 winning config, which had NO favorite lane). Favorites 0.85+ = win-11%/lose-90% payoff-trap, b=0.13, need 88% WR, −$448 all-time. Under `risk` = HOT-RELOADABLE (no restart). Set true to re-enable. Read by sol_macro + bitcoin _favorite_lane_signals.
config/settings.yaml:2516:  rsi_fade:                # 2026-08-10 RSI-GATED COINFLIP FADE (operator GO — the MEASURED >coinflip edge, project_rsi_fade_edge_found_2026_08_10). Under `risk` so it's HOT-RELOADABLE => REVERT TRIGGER = flip enabled:false (no restart) if fade-WR < breakeven. Read by sol_macro._resolve_alt_bias_for_tf (shared by ALL alts + eth): fades the direction-lane side when RSI < rsi_below AND trend NOT fully-aligned (align-gate = regime safety; fading a strong aligned trend gets run over). Favorites bypass the resolver = UNAFFECTED. Measured: RSI<40 native 30%WR => FADE 69.6% (4 sessions, never <56%). rsi_above 101 = overbought-fade OFF (ship strongest zone first). side_source retagged *_rsi_fade for attribution/monitoring.
config/settings.yaml:2517:    enabled: false   # 2026-08-11 REVERT-TRIGGER HIT (hot, no restart). LIVE session: fade 43%WR, -$90 of a -$105 loss; hype = 13/24 longs faded into a DOWN tape (RSI<40 flips short->long = buying the falling knife), -$52 of hype's -$67. The 69.6%WR was measured in an UP/chop tape; in this down tape the align-gate isn't catching the trend and the fade is anti-edge. Re-enable when the tape is choppy/ranging, NOT trending down.
config/settings.yaml:2521:    flat_edge: 0.05          # 2026-08-10 fade sizes on THIS flat edge, NOT est_prob (which is anti-predictive in the band). The fade is exempted from lane_min_edge + est_prob conviction floors (sol_macro scan loop) because est_prob-edge is ~0/NEGATIVE by construction on the faded side => without this the fade takes ZERO trades (measured: 74 resolutions -> 0 fills). Conservative 0.05 (below alt_1h_simple_long 0.06). Hot-reloadable. Set higher to size faded bets up once WR confirms.
config/settings.yaml:2522:  max_concurrent_positions: 50   # 2026-08-08 NOW HOT-RELOADABLE (operator): raise/lower the max simultaneous OPEN trades in settings.yaml and it applies live WITHOUT restart (can_trade reads it from self.config each check; "risk" is in _HOT_RELOAD_TOP_LEVEL_KEYS). NOTE: 50 is high vs a $1k bankroll at $70/favorite — lower it here anytime to cap concurrent exposure. Per-strategy override: strategies.<name>.max_concurrent_positions.
config/settings.yaml:2541:  max_same_side_notional_usd: 0.0   # 2026-08-10 SAME-SIDE $-CAP (operator GO, Codex-verified). Downsize-to-fit: cap total same-outcome (YES/NO) OPEN notional at $125/side (~12% of $1k same-direction) — crypto lanes ~90% correlated so N same-side = 1 leveraged bet (corr peak-ss-notional vs maxDD ~0.7). ⚠️ DRAWDOWN INSURANCE not EV: Codex 12-sess replay ~halves worst session (−$141→~−$91) but trims near-breakeven net slightly neg (shrinks winning clusters too). 0=off. VALUE hot-reloads (exposure); the code path in clob_client.evaluate_entry is restart-class. See project_same_side_concurrency_is_edge_not_leak_2026_08_10.
