   280	        # The two existing favorite exits both leave the SMALLEST loss at ~-$30: hold_catastrophic
   281	        # can't even trigger until the mark hits entry*(1-0.55)~0.38 (a -55% loss), and the presettle
   282	        # de-risk only fires in the final _fav_presettle_secs. So a favorite winning +8..18% pays a
   283	        # -30..-66 loser — break-even needs ~80% WR (measured 81% WR still -$43/session). This cuts a
   284	        # favorite the moment its our-side mark walks down to hard_stop_price at ANY point in the hold,
   285	        # capping the loss early (0.70 from 0.87 = -20%, not -55%): break-even WR = (p-x)/(1-x) falls
   286	        # 79%->57%. 0.70 sits DEEP inside the plausible band (delta 0.17 << 0.50) so it fires on the
   287	        # real walk-down, never on an inverted/junk print. OFF unless favorite_lane.hard_stop_price>0.
